<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rajah Sulayman</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1571">1571</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Sulayman III</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Rajah Sulayman was a ruler of Maynila who shared power with his uncle <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajah-matanda">Rajah Matanda</a> in the 16th century. He resisted the Spanish, and after a clash in 1570 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/martin-de-goiti">Martín de Goiti</a> burned the town. When <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/miguel-lopez-de-legazpi">Miguel López de Legazpi</a> founded Spanish <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manila">Manila</a> in 1571, Sulayman led a coalition against them and was killed at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-bangkusay-channel">Battle of Bangkusay</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rajah-sulayman.jpg" alt="Rajah Sulayman" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ralff Nestor Nacor · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rajah_Sulayman_Monument,_Malate,_Manila.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
